<title>CANADA: IMAX in US$35.2 mln bought deal.</title>
<headline>IMAX in US$35.2 mln bought deal.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imax Corp said on Wednesday that a group of its shareholders entered a bought deal financing agreement with Nesbitt Burns Inc and Toronto-Dominion Securities to issue US$35.2 million worth of common shares at US$22 a share.</p>
<p>The two underwriting firms agreed to offer the shares for sale to the public in Canada.</p>
<p>Imax said the deal was expected to close on June 20.</p>
<p>Nesbitt Burns is the brokerage arm of Bank of Montreal, while Toronto-Dominion Securities is a unit of Toronto-Dominion Bank.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
